Muster: format any screen and terminal state, and read state Muster needs

Muster replays a pane's terminal into a fresh one when a surface attaches
(docs/mip/0003-own-daemon.md, section 5). The C formatter reaches only the
active screen and always emits content with the terminal's extras, so it
cannot reproduce the primary screen while a program holds the alternate
one, and cannot emit tabstops, the scrolling region or the pen apart from
content. This adds, in src/terminal/c/muster.zig and its header
include/ghostty/vt/muster.h, built only on the formatter's public Zig
types:

- ghostty_terminal_format_screen: a ScreenFormatter for the primary or
  alternate screen, with all its rows, the active area only (how a
  surface that fell behind is caught up), or the history only, which
  ends at the row above the active area exactly.
- ghostty_terminal_format_state: the terminal's extras with no content,
  then the active screen's, with the cursor placed for the receiver's
  origin mode and right margin whether or not the modes extra is asked
  for. TerminalFormatter sets cursor_origin and wrap_column only when it
  emits the modes itself; Muster writes modes on its own, and a pending
  wrap at a blank cell is lost without them.

It also adds terminal state the C API does not reach:

- ghostty_terminal_screen_cursor_style: either screen's cursor style.
  DECSCUSR sets the active screen's only, and the render state reads
  only the active one.
- ghostty_terminal_mouse_tracking: the tracking mode and format in
  effect, which the mode bits cannot say, since setting a tracking mode
  replaces the last without clearing its bit.
- ghostty_terminal_mouse_shift_capture: what XTSHIFTESCAPE set.
- ghostty_terminal_clear_screen: the terminal half of Ghostty's own
  clear_screen binding (Termio.clearScreen), for a daemon that performs
  the binding on a terminal with no Termio.
- ghostty_terminal_kitty_image_loading, _loading_bytes and
  _drop_loading: whether a chunked kitty image is still arriving, how
  much of it has, and dropping it. A program cut off between two chunks
  leaves its image arriving until a full reset.

Additive only: a new file and header plus their export lines; no
existing behavior changed and no formatter code touched, so a re-pin
rebases the export lines only. Muster carries this for good rather than
sending it upstream. The Zig tests at the end of src/terminal/c/muster.zig
cover it: zig build test-lib-vt -Dtest-filter=muster.

